# The GitHub "Source code" zip/tar.gz and the "Download ZIP" button are both
# `git archive` output: no .git, so `git describe` has nothing to read. This
# makes git substitute the version into the file at archive time instead, so a
# downloaded copy still reports what produced it. See lib/version.py.
#
# Keep this scoped to the one file. export-subst rewrites every matched file in
# full, so widening it would expand placeholder-shaped text anywhere in the tree
# -- including the test that asserts the placeholder is *un*expanded.
lib/version.py export-subst
